# Intentionally empty -- no "auto" stanza, so S40network's "ifup -v -a"
# leaves usb0 alone.
#
# The usbnet package installs an "auto usb0 / iface usb0 inet dhcp" stanza
# in its default (no-NCM) branch, and usbnet is force-selected by
# BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_KOPT_DWC2_OTG, which we need for USB device mode.
# The g_webcam composite on this kernel DOES include an NCM function
# (host side: "cdc_ncm 3-1.1.4:1.6"), so usb0 exists here -- but this
# board is deliberately UVC-only, there is no DHCP server on the other
# end, and the stanza just leaves a udhcpc broadcasting DISCOVER forever.
#
# Delete this file to re-enable USB networking.
